# Observability

Production code must be diagnosable.

- Use structured logs.
- Do not log secrets or tokens.
- Propagate correlation identifiers.
- Emit meaningful technical and business metrics.
- Trace cross-service flows when useful.
- Create actionable alarms around user-visible or service-level failures.
- Make asynchronous failure and dead-letter states visible.
- Include enough context to diagnose failures without exposing sensitive information.

Observability requirements should be considered during design, not added after implementation.
